WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.800
The circle closes. Remington,
who had painted cavalry charges on the Plains,

2
00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:09.760
now painted Theodore Roosevelt's Rough Riders
charging the San Juan Heights in Cuba,

3
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.290
on July first, 1898.

4
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.030
He was there as a war correspondent.

5
00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:19.650
The composition is built
like his frontier scenes: heroic figures,

6
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:23.490
forward momentum, a triumph
that seems meant to be.

7
00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:26.580
But look closely.
Most of the men are on foot,

8
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.160
because their horses had been left
behind in Florida.

9
00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:32.790
And they actually charged
nearby Kettle Hill.

10
00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:35.330
The legend was bigger than the battle.
